{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueHabiroDual","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueHabiroDual","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residue_vs_alphaEm_at_bar_antifixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residue_vs_alphaEm_at_bar_antifixed","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L118-L127","doc":"**Zero/non-vanishing duality at the bar-antifixed locus, packaged.** At\n`qi = −q`: the α_EM factor `[2]_q` is zero, while the Q_β residue numerator `N`\nequals `2q(1 − 4q²α)` (non-zero under `residueNum_ne_zero_at_bar_antifixed`'s\nhypotheses). So `[2]_q`'s vanishing is α_EM's **zero** in the bar-even sector and\nthe **pole** of `F = N/[2]_q` in the bar-odd sector — two faces of the same\nfactor. (Equalities only; non-vanishing/pole are the separate lemma + caveat.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residueNum_ne_zero_at_bar_antifixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residueNum_ne_zero_at_bar_antifixed","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L105-L116","doc":"**The residue numerator is genuinely NON-zero at the bar-antifixed locus**,\nunder explicit non-vanishing hypotheses on its two factors (stated over a domain\nso `mul_ne_zero` applies). Combined with `bracketTwo_zero_at_bar_antifixed`\n(`[2]_q = 0` there), this is the rigorous content of \"`F = N/[2]_q` has a pole\":\nthe denominator vanishes while the numerator does not — a genuine singularity in\nany localisation inverting `[2]_q`. (We do not formalise the pole as a fraction-\nfield object; this `≠ 0` + `= 0` pair is the CommRing-level statement.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residueNum_at_bar_antifixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residueNum_at_bar_antifixed","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L97-L103","doc":"**Evaluation of the residue numerator at the bar-antifixed locus**:\n`N(q, −q, α) = 2q·(1 − 4q²·α)`. (A `ring` identity; the non-vanishing and pole\nreadings are separate — see `residueNum_ne_zero_at_bar_antifixed` and the\ndocstring's pole caveat.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.bracketTwo_zero_at_bar_antifixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.bracketTwo_zero_at_bar_antifixed","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L90-L95","doc":"**`[2]_q` vanishes at the bar-antifixed locus `qi = −q`.** After specialising\n`qi = q⁻¹` this is the ζ₄ condition `q + q⁻¹ = 0`; since `[2]_q` is a *factor* of\nα_EM, the same locus is α_EM's modular **zero**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residueNum_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residueNum_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L79-L88","doc":"**The Q_β residue numerator is bar-ODD under the swap**:\n`N(qi, q, α) = −N(q, qi, α)` (recovering `N(q⁻¹) = −N(q)` after specialising\n`qi = q⁻¹`). This is the structural complement of α_EM's\n`alphaEmHabiro_bar_invariant` (bar-EVEN, `H(qi,q) = H(q,qi)`): the Q_β residue\nlives in the bar-ANTIsymmetric sector (PR #1900, PR #1907), which is exactly why\nit required a separate cancellation analysis rather than a Habiro-fixed-point\nidentification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.heckeDiff_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.heckeDiff_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L74-L77","doc":"**`h` is bar-ODD** — flips sign under the swap `q ↔ qi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.bracketTwo_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.bracketTwo_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L69-L72","doc":"**`[2]_q` is bar-EVEN** — invariant under the swap `q ↔ qi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residueNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.residueNum","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L64-L67","doc":"The Q_β residue-A **numerator** `N = h·(1 − h²α)` — the bar-ODD dual of the\nα_EM factor `[2]_q·(1 − h²α)`. The residue element is `F = N / [2]_q` (singular\nat the `[2]_q` zero). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.heckeDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.heckeDiff","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L61-L62","doc":"bar-ODD Hecke differential `h = q − qi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.bracketTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaResidueDual.bracketTwo","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaResidueHabiroDual.lean#L56-L59","doc":"bar-EVEN generator `[2]_q = q + qi` (the α_EM prefactor; its zero locus is\nthe bar-antifixed locus, which is the ζ₄ pole locus of the dual after\nspecialising `qi = q⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}